.TH PAM_FACEAUTH 8 "2026-11" "faceauth 0.10.0" "Linux-PAM Manual"
.SH NAME
pam_faceauth \- PAM module for face authentication
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B auth sufficient pam_faceauth.so
.RI [ timeout=N ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pam_faceauth
asks
.BR faceauth-daemon (8)
to match the face of
.B PAM_USER
against that user's enrolled face data. On a match it returns
.BR PAM_SUCCESS ;
on every other outcome it returns
.B PAM_AUTHINFO_UNAVAIL
so the stack continues with the next module, normally the password prompt.
.PP
The module is skipped without opening the camera when:
.IP \(bu 2
.B PAM_RHOST
is set (remote login);
.IP \(bu 2
the session of the calling process is remote, has no seat, or is not the
foreground session (SSH, including sudo inside SSH; remote desktop;
switched-away users). A process outside any logind session (for example a
terminal started by the systemd user manager) is judged instead by the
session of the process connected to its standard input, if that is a Unix
socket (polkit's socket-activated agent helper, connected to the user's
polkit agent), or else by the invoking user's graphical session, as polkit
does;
.IP \(bu 2
neither exists (cron jobs, system services);
.IP \(bu 2
the PAM service is not listed in
.BR faceauth.conf (5)
or the user disabled it;
.IP \(bu 2
the service is a graphical login screen
.RB ( gdm-password ", " gdm-autologin ", " sddm ", " lightdm ", " cosmic-greeter )
and the user's session is not locked: these only unlock;
.IP \(bu 2
the user has no enrolled face, the enrolled camera is not connected, is
virtual, or is not IR while
.B require_ir
is set.
.PP
After repeated immediate failures (a lock screen retrying), the daemon waits
up to 20 seconds before turning on the camera.
.PP
The module connects to the system bus at its fixed socket path and ignores
.BR DBUS_SYSTEM_BUS_ADDRESS ,
which is controlled by the invoking user in setuid programs.
.PP
The module starts no processes. While the camera runs, the user's session
agent (faceauth-agent, started by XDG autostart) shows a desktop
notification on the daemon's behalf.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI timeout= N
Authentication timeout in seconds (1 to 30). Default: the
.B timeout
setting of
.BR faceauth.conf (5).
.SH MODULE TYPES PROVIDED
.B auth
only.
.B pam_setcred
returns success and does nothing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# /etc/pam.d/sudo, before the password module
auth  sufficient  pam_faceauth.so
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR faceauth (1),
.BR faceauth.conf (5),
.BR faceauth-daemon (8),
.BR pam (8)
